			"meta": {
				"abilities": [
					{
						"description": "At the start of your Command phase, you can select one combat doctrine listed below. If you do, that combat doctrine is active for friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES units with this ability until the start of your next Command phase.\nASSAULT DOCTRINEWhen this unit is selected to make an advance move, that advance move does not prevent this unit from being eligible to declare a charge.\nDEVASTATOR DOCTRINEThis unit's ranged attacks have [ASSAULT].\nTACTICAL DOCTRINEWhen this unit is selected to make a fall-back move, that fall-back move does not prevent this unit from being eligible to shoot and eligible to declare a charge.\nUnless otherwise stated:\n• You can only select each combat doctrine once per battle.\n• Only one combat doctrine can be active for each unit. If a rule makes a combat doctrine active for a unit, any combat doctrine previously active for that unit is no longer active for that unit.",
						"name": "Combat Doctrines",
						"type": "Faction"
					},
					{
						"description": "Before this model is removed from play:\n  -> Roll one D6: on a 6+, each enemy unit within 6\" suffers 1 mortal wound.",
						"name": "Deadly Demise 1",
						"type": "Core"
					},
					{
						"description": "The unit has the Feel No Pain 6+ ability.",
						"name": "Feel No Pain 6+",
						"type": "Core"
					},
					{
						"description": "While this unit is within 6\" of a friendly SPACE WOLVES CHARACTER model (excluding WULFEN models) or within 12\" of a friendly WOLF PRIEST model, if this unit is not battle-shocked:\n• If this unit has INFANTRY, this unit has +1 OC.\n• If this unit has VEHICLE, this unit has +3 OC.\nBestial Forms: For the purposes of transport capacity, each WULFEN model takes up the space of 2 models.",
						"name": "Curse of the Wulfen",
						"type": "Faction"
					},
					{
						"description": "If this model is equipped with two melee weapons, melee attacks made by this unit have [TWIN-LINKED].",
						"name": "Violent Fury",
						"type": "Datasheet"
					},
					{
						"description": "In your opponent's Shooting phase, when an enemy unit has shot, if this unit lost a wound as a result of those attacks, this unit can make a surge move of up to D6+1\".",
						"name": "Bestial Rage",
						"type": "Datasheet"
					}
				],
